~~~java
OrderDto find(long id) {
    return repository.findById(id)
        .map(mapper::toDto)
        .orElseThrow(() -> new OrderNotFound(id));
}
~~~

The repository says only whether the entity exists. The service chooses a domain meaning for absence. A RestControllerAdvice can map OrderNotFound to 404. In a batch process, the same empty result might instead be skipped or recorded. This separation is why 'orElseThrow is best for REST' is too broad: the correct operation depends on the use case and error contract.

