```java
@Entity
public class Order implements Persistable<UUID> {
    @Id private UUID id;
    @Transient private boolean isNew = true; // not persisted

    @Override public UUID getId() { return id; }
    @Override public boolean isNew() { return isNew; }

    @PostLoad @PostPersist
    void markNotNew() { this.isNew = false; }
}
// Now save() trusts isNew() -> persist() -> straight INSERT, no SELECT.
```
For auto-generated IDs you don't need this — a null id already signals "new".

```java
@Service
public class ProductService {
    private final ProductRepository repository;
    ProductService(ProductRepository r) { this.repository = r; }

    public Product create(String name, BigDecimal price) {
        var p = new Product();
        p.setName(name);
        p.setPrice(price);
        return repository.save(p); // id null -> persist() -> INSERT (id filled)
    }

    @Transactional
    public Product updatePrice(Long id, BigDecimal price) {
        var p = repository.findById(id).orElseThrow();
        p.setPrice(price);
        return p; // managed -> dirty checking -> UPDATE at commit (no save needed)
    }
}
